# Specialist routing

**Zero-hop by default.** Every `Task(subagent)` call is a full extra agent turn (new context, tools, Lifecycle report) — expensive and slow. The parent Auto session does the work itself unless the user explicitly names a specialist. Do not auto-invoke a subagent just because a task "belongs" to a domain.

Wiring metadata (invoke phrases, dashboards, handoffs) for opt-in specialists lives in `.cursor/agent-system/registry.json` — do not duplicate full agent prompts here. Specialist specs, memories, and continuity MDCs remain useful reading (ownership rules, prior findings, deterministic checks) even when a specialist isn't invoked — the parent should still follow the relevant continuity rule for the domain it's working in.

## Before substantive work

1. **Explicit specialist ask** (e.g. "Use the ibkr-ops subagent to diagnose IB Gateway") → invoke that subagent with its registered phrase. This is the only path that opens a hop.
2. **Everything else — including "just get this done" and multi-domain work** → the parent works in-session. For multi-domain work, sequence the steps yourself in one session and follow each domain's continuity rule (see Defaults below for which file governs which area); write one aggregate task narrative when done.
3. **"Who owns X / what's cracked?"** → run `py -3 tools/agent_fleet.py` first (no LLM hop, deterministic). Only invoke `router` if the user explicitly asks for a routing card.
4. **"What's on the to-do / what's missing / priorities?"** → `py -3 tools/deferred_log.py status` (alias `priorities`). Source of truth is GitHub Issues labeled `deferred`. Do not invent a second tracker. Roadmap NEXT stays in `Nova-Roadmap-Status.md`.
5. **Before any fix** → run that command and search open `deferred` issues for the symptom/module. If an existing issue already covers the ask: **work from that issue**. Honor **Status** (`parked` means do not start it), **Unblock**, and **Next**. Do not start a parallel fix that ignores the issue.

## Defaults (ownership guidance, not auto-invoke targets)

These name which rules/files govern a domain and which specialist exists for an **explicit** ask — they are not automatic dispatch targets:

| Need | Follow / owner | Notes |
|------|-------|-------|
| Fleet triage / classification / crack index only | `router` (explicit ask) or `py -3 tools/agent_fleet.py` (default, no hop) | Dashboard = `agent-router`; report-only Routing card |
| Product change verification (pytest / Vitest / Playwright / browser) | `tester` (explicit ask) or run the commands yourself | After code changes; before claiming done |
| Maintainability / danger audit | `maintainer` (explicit ask) | Read-only; significant diffs |
| Full-repository security posture / SEC-NNN | `security` (explicit ask) | Not for PR/diff review |
| Docs, MDC rules, agent prompts, canvases, agent dreaming | `docs` (explicit ask) | Dashboard = Nova Home; `tools/agent_dream.py` |
| Webull-to-Nova widget mapping or selected parity gap | `widgets` (explicit ask) | Dashboard = `agent-widgets`; Webull evidence is research-only |
| Trading execution ADR 007 / ledger / latency / auto_live NO-GO | `execution` (explicit ask) | Audit-only; `execution-continuity.mdc`; dashboard `agent-execution` |
| IB Gateway login / IBC / API port health | `ibkr-ops` (explicit ask) | Loud-warn protocol; never stores credentials |
| General scanner L1 + quote/chart/L2/T&S coherence | `market-feed` (explicit ask) | `single-market-data-feed.mdc`; hand off HOD pool to `hod-momo`, UI layout to `widgets` |
| News / catalyst pipeline | `news` (explicit ask) | `backend/news/` + News UI |
| Hotkeys / Nova Actions / DAS `.htk` (Phase G3) | `hotkeys` (explicit ask) | Typed actions only; no raw DAS exec; `hotkeys-continuity.mdc` |
| Backtest product (Phase E) + VectorBT skill cluster | `backtester` (explicit ask) | Metrics-only; skills research/offline |
| PR / branch / uncommitted diff security | Cursor `security-review` (explicit ask) | Built-in; never swap with security |

## Continuity-only / unowned domains

If `Agent-Fleet-Map.md` marks a domain `Continuity-only` or `Unowned`, say so explicitly and work it yourself in-session following whatever partial continuity exists — do not silently absorb large, ambiguous product work without naming the gap. Scaffold a specialist via `tools/create_nova_agent.py` when a domain keeps burning sessions.

## Invoke (explicit opt-in only)

Use each agent's registered phrases from the registry (also listed in the agent spec under **Invoke phrases**). Example: “Use the tester subagent to verify …”

## Lifecycle

Every Nova specialist report must end with:

```text
**Lifecycle:** memory=unchanged|changed | promotion=none|<what> | dashboard=clean|refresh-required | handoff=none|<sibling|parent> | task_log=<path>|skipped|n/a | deferred_log=<id>|none|skipped|n/a
```

`task_log=` is required after material work: fill the PR body (`.github/pull_request_template.md`) and cite its URL, or write `knowledge/task-log/YYYY-MM-DD-*.md` when the work ships without a PR (see `.cursor/rules/task-log.mdc`), or `skipped` / `n/a` with a brief reason when the skip rules apply. The parent must ensure one aggregate narrative exists for multi-domain work done in-session.


`deferred_log=` is **mandatory for every agent** (see `.cursor/rules/deferred-log.mdc`): after parking a known bug or a feature you will not build this session, open or update a GitHub Issue labeled `deferred` and set `deferred_log=#NNN` (its GitHub number); otherwise `none` / `skipped` / `n/a`. Silent omission after parking real work is a constitution violation. Do not dump parked work only into agent-memory Backlog.

The `subagentStop` hook (`.cursor/hooks.json`) may remind once if the footer is missing. It is fail-open and never edits files.

## Ops

See `docs/agent-operations.md`. Validate with `py -3 tools/agent_contract.py`.

## Repository boundary

Personal course libraries, authenticated-site notes, and generated research graphs live outside this repository. Do not recreate or publish them here. Scanner diagnostics use Nova and IBKR evidence.
